{"id":"NCT05064540","title":"JAGUAR Trial: ObJective Analysis to GaUge EVAR Outcomes Through Randomization","official":"JAGUAR Trial: ObJective Analysis to GaUge EVAR Outcomes Through Randomization","summary":"Prospective, randomized, multi-center study designed to evaluate the outcomes of commercially available contemporary EVAR in a real-world population. Patients will be randomized into two device cohorts and compared across the primary endpoints.\n\nPatients will be followed procedurally to discharge, at 1, 6, 12 months and annually through to 5 years (total follow-up commitment).","conditions":["AAA","AAA - Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm"],"interventions":[{"type":"DEVICE","name":"Alto Abdominal Stent Graft System"},{"type":"DEVICE","name":"FDA Approved EVAR AAA Graft Systems"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Adult age 21 and older\n* Subjects with minimum of 2 year life expectancy\n* Subjects have signed the informed consent document\n* Subjects with unruptured infrarenal AAA who are assessed by the Investigator to be eligible for endovascular Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm Repair with the trial devices.\n* Patient must be able and willing to comply with all required follow-up exams.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Currently participating in another trial where the primary endpoint has not been reached yet.\n* Known allergy to any of the device components\n* Pregnant (females of childbearing potential only)\n* Known connective tissue disorders\n* Known active infection\n* Subjects with pre-existing EVAR, i.e., in need of repair/intervention of a previously failed EVAR.\n* Patient has other medical, social, or psychological conditions that, in the opinion of the investigator, preclude them from receiving the pre-treatment, required treatment, and post-treatment procedures and evaluations.","minAge":"21 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":450,"start":"2021-09-20","pcd":"2032-03","upd":"2026-09-09","sponsor":"Endologix","areas":["other"],"central":["Noel DeSisto · 864-270-8524 · ndesisto@endologix.com","Sanjana Tabassum · stabassum@endologix.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Huntsville Hospital","city":"Huntsville","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35801","s":"ANR","lat":34.7304,"lon":-86.5859,"c":""},{"f":"University of Arizona","city":"Tucson","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85716","s":"R","lat":32.2217,"lon":-110.9265,"c":"Karen Sanchez · kas10@arizona.edu"},{"f":"Washington Regional Medical Center","city":"Fayetteville","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72703","s":"R","lat":36.0626,"lon":-94.1574,"c":"Callie McQueen · 479-463-7858 · cmcqueen@wregional.com"},{"f":"Central Arkansas Veterans Healthcare System","city":"Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72205","s":"R","lat":34.7465,"lon":-92.2896,"c":"Sandra Brock · 501-257-6906 · sandra.brock@va.gov"},{"f":"The Regents of the University of California, San Diego","city":"La Jolla","pr":"California","zip":"92093","s":"R","lat":32.8473,"lon":-117.2742,"c":"Kathleen Groh · (951)595-2347 · kagroh@health.ucsd.edu"},{"f":"Veterans Affairs San Diego Healthcare System","city":"San Diego","pr":"California","zip":"92161","s":"R","lat":32.7157,"lon":-117.1647,"c":"Annalicia Vargas · annalicia.vargas@va.gov"},{"f":"MedStar Washington Hospital Center","city":"Washington D.C.","pr":"District of Columbia","zip":"20001","s":"R","lat":38.8951,"lon":-77.0364,"c":"Kassaye Sesaba · 202-877-7452 · Kassaye.T.Sesaba@medstar.net"},{"f":"Jacksonville Center for Clinical Research","city":"Jacksonville","pr":"Florida","zip":"32216","s":"R","lat":30.3322,"lon":-81.6556,"c":"Lisa Joseph · 904.732.2217 · ljoseph@encoredocs.com"},{"f":"Radiology and Imaging Specialists","city":"Lakeland","pr":"Florida","zip":"33801","s":"R","lat":28.0395,"lon":-81.9498,"c":"Eve Johnson · 863-688-2334 ext. 135 · ejohnson@risimaging.com"},{"f":"Baptist Hospital of Miami, Miami Cardiac and Vascular Institute","city":"Miami","pr":"Florida","zip":"33176","s":"R","lat":25.7743,"lon":-80.1937,"c":"David Fe